{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tourmaline-obese-cusimanse","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The deterministic child-closure proof is computed, then hidden from the verifier\n\nThe completion precheck already computes, deterministically and exactly, whether every direct child\nof a parent is closed and certified — `child_closure_findings(ticket)` returns\n`(blocking, uncertified)`. For epic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb] this is measured as\n`blocking=0, uncertified=0`: hard proof that all 59 descendants are closed AND carry certified\nsignatures.\n\nThat proof is then **collapsed to a single boolean** (`certifiable`) at\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py:132` and routed only to the `reconcile` step. **Nothing about it\nreaches the verifier's prompt** — `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/completion-verification.yaml` wires\nonly `context` into the `decide@then/verify` step.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nEpics routinely write an acceptance criterion of the form *\"every child story is closed and its\nchange is `Verified +1` on Gerrit\"* (e369's criterion #1, verbatim). The verifier is handed that\ncriterion with **zero evidence**, and it has no tool that can reach the answer:\n\n* the **closure/certification half** is already proven deterministically one step earlier and is\n  discarded;\n* the **Gerrit half** (`Verified +1`) is not obtainable from the repository at all — no read-only\n  repo tool can query Gerrit.\n\nSo the verifier must either guess, or follow its own instruction\n(`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md:150-151`: *\"If, after a bounded search, you cannot\nfind evidence that a requirement is met, record what you searched and treat it as NOT MET\"*) and\nFAIL a criterion that is in fact satisfied and was **already proven satisfied by deterministic code\nin the same workflow run**. That is a false FAIL on a gate that SIGNS its verdict.\n\nIt also wastes budget: the verifier spends tool calls hunting for evidence that no tool can produce.\n\n## Discovered from\n\n[rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e] — while root-causing why e369's completion verification never reaches a\nverdict. Recorded there and in [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a]'s RCA as the most likely route to a\ngenuine FAIL even once the run does reach a verdict.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the deterministic child-closure/certification result (counts, and the ids of any\n      unclosed/uncertified children) is surfaced to the completion verifier as evidence, inside the\n      existing fenced-context delimiter so it keeps the prompt-injection boundary\n- [ ] a criterion of the form \"every child is closed\" can be resolved from that evidence without the\n      verifier making a tool call\n- [ ] the Gerrit half (`Verified +1`) is explicitly addressed: either evidence is supplied, or the\n      verifier is told plainly that this half is out of reach so it does not silently FAIL on it\n- [ ] a test pins that the evidence appears in the verify step's inputs and that its content matches\n      what `child_closure_findings` returned\n- [ ] no change to the deterministic short-circuit: an UNCLOSED direct child must still block with no\n      LLM call","id":"6ec8-24c7-182b-40d0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Child-closure proof is computed deterministically then hidden from the completion verifier"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785942963040810001,"uuid":"02506b87-768b-4ed5-a3a7-e177dc1455cb"}